{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, it wouldn't be technology or politics or money.\n\nIt would be this: **I'd make empathy automatic.**\n\nNot the idea of empathy that we talk about, but the real, visceral feeling of it. For a moment, you would actually *feel* what it's like to be the other person - the tired cashier, the parent you disagree with, the stranger on the other side of the world, the person who hurt you.\n\nNot mind-reading. Just a brief, undeniable moment of \"Oh, this is what it feels like to live inside their life.\"\n\nI think almost everything that breaks the world - war, cruelty, loneliness, the way we trash the planet - comes from a failure of imagination. We can't really picture that other people are as real, as complicated, as scared and hopeful as we are.\n\nIf we could feel it for even 10 seconds, you couldn't dehumanize anyone. You couldn't leave a child hungry if you felt his hunger in your own stomach. You couldn't stay in an echo chamber if you actually felt the fear that makes someone else cling to theirs.\n\nWe wouldn't need to force people to be kinder. People *want* to be kind when they actually understand each other. We'd just finally have the information we were missing.\n\nWhat would you change, if you had the one wish?",
